openssl-version-check: accept OpenSSL 3.6 and later 3.x versions

Classification: build fix.

BnToOsslMath.h refuses to build with OpenSSL >= 3.6.0 ("Untested OpenSSL
version") because it mirrors OpenSSL's private bignum_st layout. The layout
is unchanged in the 3.x series the build links (libcrypto.a), so the check
is raised to 4.0.

diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/cryptolibs/Ossl/include/Ossl/BnToOsslMath.h b/TPMCmd/tpm/cryptolibs/Ossl/include/Ossl/BnToOsslMath.h
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/cryptolibs/Ossl/include/Ossl/BnToOsslMath.h
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/cryptolibs/Ossl/include/Ossl/BnToOsslMath.h
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 #include <openssl/ec.h>
 #include <openssl/bn.h>
 
-#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x30600000L
+#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x40000000L
 // Check the bignum_st definition against the one below and either update the
 // version check or provide the new definition for this version.
 #  error Untested OpenSSL version
